        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7a889f14-3acd-3dce-a47f-31815a4a86da",
                "word": "versmachten",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f139766-c7e6-3786-94a7-9ea39539b5cf",
                        "entry_id": "7a889f14-3acd-3dce-a47f-31815a4a86da",
                        "glosses": [
                            "in heel sterke mate lijden"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "af218dde-34e1-42cf-bd4a-0bcba121acc0",
                                "sense_id": "6f139766-c7e6-3786-94a7-9ea39539b5cf",
                                "text": "Pippi: 'Schrijf maar op, Tommy. We zitten hier al dagen zonder snuif en versmachten.'Tommy: 'Maar dat is toch onzin, Pippi. Wij gebruiken toch zeker helemaal geen snuif.'Pippi: 'Luister goed Tommy. Ik leg het maar één keer uit. Wie zitten er vaker zonder snuif: zij die snuif gebruiken of zij die nooit snuif gebruiken?'Tommy: 'Tsja, zij die nooit snuif gebruiken, natuurlijk.'Pippi: 'Nou dan. Schrijf dus maar op: we zitten hier al dagen zonder snuif en versmachten.'Waarna Tommy het braaf noteert, de brief in de fles stopt, de kurk erop draait en het geheel aan Pippi overhandigt die het met een reuzenzwaai in het hen omringende meer gooit."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b8b66ee6-208d-3d77-8896-7bc0bbd9c06d",
                        "entry_id": "7a889f14-3acd-3dce-a47f-31815a4a86da",
                        "glosses": [
                            "zo erg lijden dat men sterft"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "74814438-fc62-4315-8b4b-7dc49ae9da2a",
                                "sense_id": "b8b66ee6-208d-3d77-8896-7bc0bbd9c06d",
                                "text": "Zoals het graf van Moeier Kraak of ook wel Moeier Neuk, die in de zeventiende eeuw aan de pest stierf, alsmede de kastanjeboom waar aan de legendarische roverhoofdman Rosse Bruno zou zijn opgehangen (Zwarte Kaat, diens zuster in het kwaad, werd 'versmacht onder een zwaar neerploffend bed')."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e5649097-b47c-3a81-b94f-5ddf0c61a8b9",
                        "entry_id": "7a889f14-3acd-3dce-a47f-31815a4a86da",
                        "glosses": [
                            "verstikking door uitwendige druk op de borstkas"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d18b5ed3-1a00-49ec-b565-b76bb920d5b4",
                        "source_entry_id": "7a889f14-3acd-3dce-a47f-31815a4a86da",
                        "source_sense_id": "b8b66ee6-208d-3d77-8896-7bc0bbd9c06d",
                        "source_sense_description": "sterven",
                        "target_lang_word": "expire",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "expire",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9bb8e88b-7ba1-3015-baf1-b31d15c50c9e",
                                        "entry_id": "271353bb-e51b-309c-8465-550c68f0bb3b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To die."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbfd8e45-a411-4f1b-9f1d-e07e8504da6b",
                                                "sense_id": "9bb8e88b-7ba1-3015-baf1-b31d15c50c9e",
                                                "text": "The patient expired in hospital."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "057e4600-68d6-4092-b009-402bee3ef0ed",
                                                "sense_id": "9bb8e88b-7ba1-3015-baf1-b31d15c50c9e",
                                                "text": "And then, his head ſinking on his pillow, he expired; at about half an hour after ten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "981d2e6b-3614-4574-80da-cd157b6978af",
                                                "sense_id": "9bb8e88b-7ba1-3015-baf1-b31d15c50c9e",
                                                "text": "Hippolita, ſcarce more alive than her daughter, was regardleſs of every thing but her: but when the tender Iſabella’s care would have likewiſe removed her, while the ſurgeons examined Matilda’s wound, ſhe cried, remove me! never! never! I lived but in her, and will expire with her."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b96692f-fa20-4cc0-aa5e-f294f2300685",
                                                "sense_id": "9bb8e88b-7ba1-3015-baf1-b31d15c50c9e",
                                                "text": "Soon the patient had no longer sufficient strength to sit up; the trunk of the body was inclined to the right side, the head high and thrown backward, the mouth wide open: she seemed to stifle rather than respire: lastly, speech and respiration failed her; she uttered, however, in a feeble voice, some incoherent words, said she felt she was dying, and, accordingly, expired the sixth day after entrance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a738a31e-f100-4f87-8376-304e33b7e086",
                                                "sense_id": "9bb8e88b-7ba1-3015-baf1-b31d15c50c9e",
                                                "text": "People bled to death like gentlemen in an operating room or expired without comment in an oxygen tent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43a1af47-2db8-36b0-a2be-07ab1b8418a3",
                                        "entry_id": "271353bb-e51b-309c-8465-550c68f0bb3b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To lapse and become invalid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f053a23-2e21-4184-83a7-23cefdcb547c",
                                                "sense_id": "43a1af47-2db8-36b0-a2be-07ab1b8418a3",
                                                "text": "My library card will expire next week."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5f1abb4f-d89d-3bb7-9954-cb9abb940c18",
                                        "entry_id": "271353bb-e51b-309c-8465-550c68f0bb3b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To come to an end; to conclude."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66b005bb-ac4f-49c6-bf84-798c4631b424",
                                                "sense_id": "5f1abb4f-d89d-3bb7-9954-cb9abb940c18",
                                                "text": "And when the thousand yeeres are expired, Satan shall be loosed out of his prison, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27689d11-047d-3328-a329-26eaa77105d1",
                                        "entry_id": "271353bb-e51b-309c-8465-550c68f0bb3b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To exhale; to breathe out."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01ebc4f0-e5c5-4c07-9897-fc0394ae8ac1",
                                                "sense_id": "27689d11-047d-3328-a329-26eaa77105d1",
                                                "text": "Anatomy exhibits the lungs in a continual motion of inspiring and expiring air."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf10b966-04e0-4422-9f77-d867a4da466d",
                                                "sense_id": "27689d11-047d-3328-a329-26eaa77105d1",
                                                "text": "This chafed the boar; his nostrils flames expire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c39b95c0-c2ed-4642-ba0f-f56636aec5ad",
                                                "sense_id": "27689d11-047d-3328-a329-26eaa77105d1",
                                                "text": "Animals expire carbon and plants inspire it; plants expire oxygen and animals inspire it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e5f27505-3c78-3697-b9b3-9b8abc3bd18f",
                                        "entry_id": "271353bb-e51b-309c-8465-550c68f0bb3b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To give forth insensibly or gently, as a fluid or vapour; to emit in minute particles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd92fd2a-0f85-41c2-b74d-5dd30da55a0f",
                                                "sense_id": "e5f27505-3c78-3697-b9b3-9b8abc3bd18f",
                                                "text": "the expiring of cold out of the inward parts of the earth in winter"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c257c86-4b25-32eb-8418-eb36bfad9dbe",
                                        "entry_id": "271353bb-e51b-309c-8465-550c68f0bb3b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To bring to a close; to terminate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7943337-f9bb-4454-be26-1115ac98cea1",
                                                "sense_id": "2c257c86-4b25-32eb-8418-eb36bfad9dbe",
                                                "text": "Expire the term / Of a despised life."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "453b3641-9fe8-44e8-a18e-5922eb9110a1",
                        "source_entry_id": "7a889f14-3acd-3dce-a47f-31815a4a86da",
                        "source_sense_id": "b8b66ee6-208d-3d77-8896-7bc0bbd9c06d",
                        "source_sense_description": "sterven",
                        "target_lang_word": "pass away",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pass away",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "994db23c-9c40-3063-ba3e-d954d1e0d0e2",
                                        "entry_id": "06358b28-74d2-3681-9fb9-98a6cc184be2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To die."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "euphemistic",
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e026670d-fff0-446f-87cf-be453cde4cce",
                                                "sense_id": "994db23c-9c40-3063-ba3e-d954d1e0d0e2",
                                                "text": "After a long battle with cancer, the professor passed away yesterday."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89d4ee05-bc47-4080-9985-6eea46c54ce0",
                                                "sense_id": "994db23c-9c40-3063-ba3e-d954d1e0d0e2",
                                                "text": "Her great grandmother passed away yesterday."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1af4ad1-35e4-46b4-bc1b-994c99b82822",
                                                "sense_id": "994db23c-9c40-3063-ba3e-d954d1e0d0e2",
                                                "text": "He was wise, for he had seen a long succession of mechanical toys arrive to boast and swagger, and by-and-by break their mainsprings and pass away."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "129d487c-f5e4-3bc2-bca8-72178b383a38",
                                        "entry_id": "06358b28-74d2-3681-9fb9-98a6cc184be2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To disappear; to cease to be; to be no more."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d1f5888-838d-464b-b56b-6b5d32009d27",
                                                "sense_id": "129d487c-f5e4-3bc2-bca8-72178b383a38",
                                                "text": "Returne with ſpeed, time paſſeth ſwift away,\nOur life is fraile, and we may dye to day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a28d7311-959e-4f2d-8381-70d0e8206176",
                                                "sense_id": "129d487c-f5e4-3bc2-bca8-72178b383a38",
                                                "text": "And there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efd3db19-b674-4ce6-9262-367aa8595271",
                                                "sense_id": "129d487c-f5e4-3bc2-bca8-72178b383a38",
                                                "text": "Though the writer has striven to dwell on aspects that have passed, or are passing away, it will be apparent that many features of Midland practice have been adopted as standard for the L.M.S.R. and other railways."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b8b08b94-1087-34b0-81d9-befde5af2fc6",
                                        "entry_id": "06358b28-74d2-3681-9fb9-98a6cc184be2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spend; to waste."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4f80585-7ebd-4b27-86a3-f1a01b6a4ec8",
                                                "sense_id": "b8b08b94-1087-34b0-81d9-befde5af2fc6",
                                                "text": "Lest she pass away the flower of her age."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
